   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## kubakub facade show (app)\n\nA projection mapping look for a whole facade from one picture: every window, door and cornice gets its own prompt,\nFlux 2 Klein repaints the facade region by region, then LTX 2.5 animates only the regions you mark - the rest of the\nbuilding stays pixel exact, so the video lines up with the real facade.\n\n**You need:** Flux 2 Klein 4B (`flux-2-klein-4b`, `qwen_3_4b`, `flux2-vae`) and LTX 2.5 (distilled int8\ntransformer, Gemma 4 text encoder, video + audio VAE, x2 spatial upscaler): sets 1 and 4 of docs/MODELS.md,\n`python tools/setup_kubakub.py` downloads them. Runs on a 12 GB GPU. Flux 3 Klein: swap nodes 10-11 (CLIP type flux3).\n\n**Do:** Queue. With empty fields it runs on the built-in sample facade (night style).\n\n**Your facade:** paste the path of your matrix / photo into `facade_file` and the folder of its masks (one PNG per\nregion, from After Effects / Houdini / Illustrator) into `masks_folder`. The rules name regions by their file names:\n`[W_F*]` = every mask whose name starts with W_F, `[group:Windows]` = a subfolder.\n\n**Rules:** `prompt` and `denoise` (how much changes) per region; `animate = on` + `video_prompt` makes it move,\n`t_start` / `t_end` in seconds, `motion` 0-1.\n"
   ],
   "title": "read me"
  }
 ],
